description:
## Context
Anchor E04-A1: `SysRoot`, counters and the fixture infrastructure. Other epics (E05, E06, E01) depend on this bead to know that `tl-collect` builds, `SysRoot`, `KeptFile`, `Counter`, `Measured`, `FdCache` and `CollectError` exist, the `owner-desktop` fixture is committed, `cargo xtask capture-fixture` works, `insta` is wired, and a proptest harness exists. The parts are built by E04-001 to E04-007; this bead adds the shared test helpers and the proptest harness, and closes the set. Sources: ADR-013 (fixtures, property tests), ADR-016, ADR-008 (counter rules), epic map section 3 (E04-A1).

## Deliverable
1. `crates/tl-collect/tests/common/mod.rs` (shared by every `tests/*.rs` file through `mod common;`):
   ```rust
   use std::path::PathBuf;
   use proptest::prelude::*;
   use tl_collect::SysRoot;

   /// <CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR>/tests/fixtures/<name>
   pub fn fixture_dir(name: &str) -> PathBuf;
   /// SysRoot::at(fixture_dir(name))
   pub fn fixture(name: &str) -> SysRoot;
   /// SysRoot::at(fixture_dir(name).join(format!("step{n}")))
   pub fn fixture_step(name: &str, n: u32) -> SysRoot;
   /// Bytes of <fixture>/<rel>; panics with the path in the message if missing (tests only).
   pub fn fixture_bytes(name: &str, rel: &str) -> Vec<u8>;
   /// Copies a fixture (or one step of it) into a fresh tempdir so a test can rewrite files in place
   /// between two samples. Symlinks are copied as symlinks.
   pub fn fixture_copy(name: &str, step: Option<u32>) -> tempfile::TempDir;
   /// Overwrites the files of `dst` with those of fixture `name` step `n`, in place (same inodes).
   pub fn apply_step(dst: &std::path::Path, name: &str, n: u32);
   /// Strategy: take `seed`, cut it at a random point, flip up to 16 random bytes, insert up to 8
   /// bytes drawn from b"\n \t():-0123456789", and sometimes append 0 to 512 random bytes.
   pub fn mutated(seed: Vec<u8>) -> impl Strategy<Value = Vec<u8>>;
   /// Strategy: 0..=8192 arbitrary bytes.
   pub fn arbitrary_bytes() -> impl Strategy<Value = Vec<u8>>;
   ```
2. `crates/tl-collect/tests/prop_system.rs`:
   - `mod common;`
   - `prop_kept_file_returns_exact_bytes`: for `mutated(fixture_bytes("owner-desktop", "proc/stat"))`, write the bytes to a temp file, `KeptFile::read` returns exactly those bytes.
   - `prop_counter_sequences`: arbitrary sequences of up to 64 `(u64 value, u64 t_ns, u32 generation)` through `Counter::update` never panic; every `Valid` rate is finite and `>= 0.0`.
   - `prop_resumed_between_no_panic`: arbitrary `Clock` pairs never panic.
   - A comment line `// Parser cases: added by E04-A3.` at the end of the file, where E04-A3 appends one case per parser.
3. No change to source files; if any E04-001 to E04-007 deliverable is missing or broken, fix it in this bead's commit and say so in the commit body.

## Acceptance Criteria
- **Given** E04-001 to E04-007 are merged **When** `cargo test -p tl-collect` runs **Then** every test passes, including `fixture_layout` and `prop_system`.
- **Given** a test file with `mod common;` **When** it calls `fixture("owner-desktop").proc_path("stat")` **Then** the path exists.
- **Given** a fixture with `step0` and `step1` **When** a test calls `fixture_copy(name, Some(0))` then `apply_step(dir, name, 1)` **Then** files under the copy have `step1` contents and the same inode numbers as before `apply_step`.
- **Given** the workspace **When** `cargo xtask capture-fixture tmp-check` runs on the owner machine **Then** it creates `tests/fixtures/tmp-check/`; delete that directory afterwards (do not commit it).
- **Given** `cargo clippy -p tl-collect --all-targets -- -D warnings` **When** it runs **Then** it passes.

## Files
- `crates/tl-collect/tests/common/mod.rs`: create
- `crates/tl-collect/tests/prop_system.rs`: create

## Tests
- `tests/prop_system.rs::prop_kept_file_returns_exact_bytes`, `::prop_counter_sequences`, `::prop_resumed_between_no_panic`.
- Helper self-checks in `tests/prop_system.rs`: `fixture_step_paths` (paths built correctly), `apply_step_keeps_inodes` (using a two-step fixture made in a tempdir inside the test).

## Cross-cutting
- Errors: N/A
- Validity: N/A
- Accessibility: N/A
- Performance: proptest default 256 cases per property; keep total `prop_system` run under 10 s.
- Privacy: tests never print fixture contents beyond what assertion failures show.

## Notes
- Phase P0: the phase-0 spike (E01) and the CPU worker (E12-A1) need this crate.
- `SysRoot` has three roots, `{ proc, sys, run }` (R-140 item 2, written by E04-002); fixtures may carry a scrubbed `run/udev/data/` directory. ADR-013's scrub list includes `ID_SERIAL`, `ID_SERIAL_SHORT` and `ID_WWN` values (replaced by `SCRUBBED`) and MAC addresses (`00:00:00:00:00:00`) (R-140 item 2, R-162).
- `apply_step` must write in place (`OpenOptions::new().write(true).truncate(true)` on the existing path), so a `KeptFile` held by a sampler sees the new content; do not delete and recreate files.
- Build rule: run every cargo command through `heavy-build`, for example `heavy-build cargo test -p tl-collect` and `heavy-build cargo clippy -p tl-collect --all-targets -- -D warnings`. Run `cargo fmt --check` too. `heavy-build` waits for the machine-wide build lock and runs the build in a memory-capped scope, so run it in the background when your tool call has a timeout. On exit 137 (OOM kill) retry once, then report. On exit 75 (low disk) stop and report.
- `tl-collect` has no async code, no runtime and no `unsafe` (ADR-001 rules 3 and 4). No `unwrap()` or `expect()` outside tests (`clippy::unwrap_used` is `warn` and CI runs clippy with `-D warnings`).
- Read `CLAUDE.md` first. Commit once with a pathspec: `git add <your files> && git commit -m "<plan key>: ..." -- <your files>`. Never a bare `git commit`.
- Privacy (R-260, R-261): capture `owner-desktop` only after E04-033 (tasklens-2dl.37) is merged; this bead depends on it. Before committing the fixture run `rg -i <your user name> crates/tl-collect/tests/fixtures/owner-desktop` and expect no output.

## Context
Network interface enumeration and classification from sysfs, so the Network pages work without NetworkManager. It gives the interface identity (netns inode, ifindex, name), the type used for the default visibility groups, and the connection state per tick. Run at start and every 5 s while network is demanded. Sources: ADR-016 (network row: ifindex from sysfs, netns inode from `/proc/self/ns/net`, `lo` never shows), PERF-054 (type rules in order, state labels), PERF-004 and R-053 (`tailscale0` is a Tunnel and shown; `docker0`, `veth*`, `br-*`, `virbr*`, `vnet*` are Virtual), ADR-003 (`DeviceIdentity::Net { netns_ino, ifindex, name }`), R-052.

## Deliverable
`crates/tl-collect/src/parse/netif.rs`:
```rust
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum IfaceKind { Ethernet, WiFi, Virtual, UsbNetwork, Bridge, Cellular, Tunnel, Other }
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum OperState { Connected, Disconnected, Testing, Dormant, NotPresent, LowerLayerDown, Unknown }
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct NetIface { pub name: Arc<str>, pub ifindex: u32, pub netns_ino: u64, pub kind: IfaceKind, pub arphrd_type: u32 }

pub const VIRTUAL_NAME_PREFIXES: [&str; 5] = ["docker", "veth", "br-", "virbr", "vnet"];
/// readlink root.proc/self/ns/net -> "net:[4026531840]" -> 4026531840
pub fn read_netns_ino(root: &SysRoot) -> Result<u64, CollectError>;
/// Every root.sys/class/net/* except loopback, sorted by name.
pub fn enumerate(root: &SysRoot, out: &mut Vec<NetIface>) -> Result<(), CollectError>;
pub fn classify(root: &SysRoot, name: &str, arphrd_type: u32) -> IfaceKind;
/// operstate + carrier mapped to PERF-054's labels.
pub fn read_oper_state(root: &SysRoot, name: &str, buf: &mut Vec<u8>) -> Measured<OperState>;
```
Rules (paths under `root.sys/class/net/<name>/`):
- `ifindex` and `type` (ARPHRD number) are decimal files. Loopback (`type` 772 or name `lo`) is left out (`lo` never shows).
- Classification, first rule that matches:
  1. name starts with one of `VIRTUAL_NAME_PREFIXES`: `Virtual` (checked first so `docker0` and `virbr0`, which also have a `bridge/` directory, stay Virtual as PERF-004 and PERF-054 state; this order is confirmed, R-162);
  2. `wireless/` exists or `phy80211` exists: `WiFi`;
  3. `bridge/` exists: `Bridge`;
  4. `tun_flags` exists or `type` is 65534: `Tunnel`;
  5. `device/driver` exists and the canonical path of `device` has a component starting with `usb`: `UsbNetwork`;
  6. name starts with `wwan` or `type` is 519: `Cellular`;
  7. `type` is 1 and `device` exists: `Ethernet`;
  8. otherwise `Other`.
- VPN and WireGuard refinement from NetworkManager `Device.DeviceType` is the engine's job (E12).
- `read_oper_state`: `operstate` `up` gives `Connected`, `down` `Disconnected`, `testing` `Testing`, `dormant` `Dormant`, `notpresent` `NotPresent`, `lowerlayerdown` `LowerLayerDown`; `unknown` gives `Connected` when `carrier` reads `1`, else `Unknown`. Read errors give `err.validity()` with value `Unknown`. One-shot reads (`read_trimmed`), at 1 Hz while network is demanded.

Hand fixture `tests/fixtures/netif-kinds/` with `proc/self/ns/net` a symlink to `net:[4026531840]` and `sys/class/net/` entries (real directories; `type` and `ifindex` in each):
`lo` (772), `eth0` (1, `device` symlink to `../../devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:1f.6`), `wlan0` (1, `phy80211` symlink, `device`), `br0` (1, `bridge/.keep`), `virbr0` (1, `bridge/.keep`), `docker0` (1, `bridge/.keep`), `veth12ab` (1), `tailscale0` (65534, `tun_flags`), `usb0` (1, `device` symlink to `../../devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:14.0/usb1/1-2/1-2:1.0`, `device/driver` symlink to `../../../bus/usb/drivers/cdc_ether`), `wwan0` (519), `dummy0` (1, no `device`). Each has `operstate`; `eth0` `up`, `wlan0` `dormant`, `dummy0` `unknown` with `carrier` `1`, `veth12ab` `unknown` with `carrier` `0`, `br0` `lowerlayerdown`.

## Acceptance Criteria
- **Given** `netif-kinds` **When** `read_netns_ino` **Then** `4026531840`.
- **Given** `netif-kinds` **When** `enumerate` **Then** `lo` is absent and the kinds are: `br0` Bridge, `docker0` Virtual, `dummy0` Other, `eth0` Ethernet, `tailscale0` Tunnel, `usb0` UsbNetwork, `veth12ab` Virtual, `virbr0` Virtual, `wlan0` WiFi, `wwan0` Cellular; each `netns_ino == 4026531840`.
- **Given** `eth0` **Then** `read_oper_state` is `Valid(Connected)`; `wlan0` `Valid(Dormant)`; `dummy0` `Valid(Connected)`; `veth12ab` `Valid(Unknown)`; `br0` `Valid(LowerLayerDown)`.
- **Given** an interface with no `operstate` file **Then** `read_oper_state` has validity `Missing`.
- **Given** `owner-desktop` **When** enumerated **Then** the result matches the insta snapshot, `tailscale0` (if present) is `Tunnel` and `docker0` (if present) is `Virtual`.

## Files
- `crates/tl-collect/src/parse/netif.rs`: replace the stub (code plus tests)
- `crates/tl-collect/tests/fixture_netif.rs`: create, plus snapshot
- `crates/tl-collect/tests/fixtures/netif-kinds/**`: create

## Tests
- `tests/fixture_netif.rs::netns_inode`, `::kinds_in_order`, `::oper_states`, `::missing_operstate`, `::owner_desktop_snapshot`.
- `src/parse/netif.rs::tests::prop_netns_link_parse_never_panics` (the `net:[N]` parser on arbitrary bytes).

## Cross-cutting
- Errors: `enumerate` fails only if `root.sys/class/net` cannot be listed; `read_netns_ino` returns `Parse { file: "/proc/self/ns/net", what: "link" }` on a bad link.
- Validity: `Valid`, `Missing`, `Restricted`, `Failed` for the state.
- Accessibility: N/A
- Performance: enumeration every 5 s; state read per demanded tick.
- Privacy: N/A

## Notes
- Visibility groups (`performance.show_network_{wired,wireless,vpn,virtual,other}`) are applied by the engine or UI from `IfaceKind`; the mapping is settled (R-162): Ethernet and USB network to Wired, Wi-Fi and Cellular to Wireless, Tunnel and VPN to VpnTunnel, Virtual and Bridge to Virtual, Other to Other. E12-014 (hjn.17) holds it.
- Multipass bridges (PERF-004): `mpqemubr` is added to `VIRTUAL_NAME_PREFIXES` once it is seen on a Multipass install (R-162, U-52). Not in this bead.
- Build rule: run every cargo command through `heavy-build cargo ...`, for example `heavy-build cargo test -p tl-collect` and `heavy-build cargo clippy -p tl-collect --all-targets -- -D warnings`. Run `cargo fmt --check` too. On exit 137 (OOM kill) retry once, then report. On exit 75 (low disk) stop and report.
- `tl-collect` has no async code, no runtime and no `unsafe` (ADR-001 rules 3 and 4). No `unwrap()` or `expect()` outside tests (`clippy::unwrap_used` is `warn` and CI runs clippy with `-D warnings`).
- Read `CLAUDE.md` first. Commit once with a pathspec: `git add <your files> && git commit -m "<plan key>: ..." -- <your files>`. Never a bare `git commit`.

## Context
Turns the empty `tl-collect` skeleton from E02-A1 into a crate with its dependency list, its module tree and its error type. Every later E04, E05 and E06 bead edits only its own module file, so this bead writes every E04 `mod` line up front and creates one-line stub files. Sources: ADR-001 (allowed dependencies, rule 3), ADR-015 (`CollectError` via `thiserror`), ADR-016 (module layout, "Restricted, not zero"), R-135, epic map section 2.

## Deliverable
