Display names (`DeviceDesc.display_name`), the plain text the catalog keeps; page headings are UI strings (PERF-008):
- disk and child: the kernel name (`nvme0n1`, `nvme0n1p2`, `dm-0`);
- interface: the interface name (`enp38s0`);
- temperature: `"<chip> <label>"` (`"k10temp Tctl"`); fan: `"<chip> fan<n>"`, or `"<chip> <label>"` when the fan has a label.

Every `DeviceDesc` carries `persistent_key` from the functions above and `net_kind: None` (E12-014 fills `net_kind` for interfaces with the R-162 visibility mapping). Battery keys (`bat:<NativePath>`) come from E12-023 and GPU keys (`gpu:<uuid or PCI slot>`) from the GPU workers (R-155 items 7 and 8).

`DeviceList.kinds`: `DISKS` for `disk_list`, `NETS` for `net_list`, `SENSORS | FANS` for `sensor_list`; each list is complete for its kinds (the reducer marks every identity of those kinds not in the list `present = false`).

