- Layout (UI-SYS-001): page root `v_flex().size_full().bg(window_bg)`, no padding. Optional strip slot first (Services filter strip, 28 px). Then the `TlTreeTable` with `HeaderLines::One` (header 28 px, `header` background, `divider` bottom border, `text_primary` `t_base` medium). Body `list_bg`, alternate rows `row_alt`. The body gets bottom padding equal to the status chip height (26 px times scale, UI-SHL-050).
- When `body()` is `Skeleton` or one of the empty states, the header still renders and the body area shows `render_skeleton` or `render_empty` (E27 body bead) instead of the `uniform_list`.
- Key contexts: the table body div has `key_context("Table")` (E18) and the frame wraps it with `key_context(key_context)` so the page context nests inside `Table`.
- Caching: the page embeds the frame root with `.cached(size_full)` (the page does this); the table body is not cached.
- `on_snapshot`: returns false unless `mask & delegate.mask()` is non-zero. Calls `query.on_snapshot`, then `state.note_data(header.validity, rows_len)`, then, only when `query.accepts(delegate.query_generation())`, `delegate.install(snap)`. Never calls `notify` itself (ADR-009: nothing notifies in render or for unrelated bits); the page notifies on true.
