Behaviour (exact):
- `copy_cell`: writes the cell text with `tl_ui::util::clipboard_write(cx, text)` (R-199), then pushes Success toast `copied_toast_text(text)`. The row and column are the ones captured at menu open (the menu passes them in). Cut rule: if the value has more than 60 chars (Unicode scalar values), keep the first 60 and append "…".
- `copy_row`: rows from `copy_rows()`; none -> Warning toast `nothing_selected`, nothing copied. Otherwise blocks joined by one blank line (`"\n\n"`). Success toast `row_ok`; clipboard write failure -> Error toast `row_failed`.
- `copy_rows_as_table`: header line = visible column labels joined by `\t`; then one line per row in view order with `write_cell` per visible column joined by `\t`; lines joined by `\n`. Tabs and newlines inside a value are replaced by one space each. Glyph cells write nothing (empty field). Same toasts as `copy_row`; with nothing selected the `nothing_selected` toast.
- One `String` per command with `capacity = rows * 256`. The data is read at command time (selection then), except `copy_cell`, which uses the row and column captured at menu open.
- Toasts go through `ToastQueue::push(kind, text, None, None)` (E16-A2) on the window that ran the command.
- Group rows are never passed (the page's `copy_rows` skips them). Services child process rows: the Services page writes the process "Copy details" block for them inside its own `write_block` (not this file's concern).

