## Context
Each admitted action is one task in the session's actions region. It emits `Started`, then one final state per target, then one summary with `target: None` (Succeeded only if every target succeeded; otherwise the worst state in the order Failed, OutcomeUnknown, Rejected), sends `ActionFinished` to the reducer, and reports `Failed(Internal("internal error"))` on a panic. Each target's blocking job runs under `time::timeout` with the ADR-006 deadline; a timeout is `OutcomeUnknown`, never `Failed`. Events are sent with a 1 s timeout and dropped when the UI is not draining. `OpsError` maps to `ActionError`. This bead also fixes the shape of the three hooks other epics fill: the privileged helper link (E29, open item E29-OI-6), the systemd manager connections (E14-001 `ManagerConnSlot`) and the session-bus openers (E14-A3). Sources: ADR-005 (event order, channel, deadlines note: service jobs have no client-side timeout), ADR-006 (deadline table, EPERM mapping), ADR-015 (`ActionError`, panic rule, action logs), API notes section 6 (one task per action, explicit timeout), R-117, R-134, E11-001, B3 open items 8 and 9.

