`MainWindow::new`: create the focus handle, `TitleBarView`, `TabStrip` (built tabs, start tab, history mode), `StatusChip`, `ToastQueue::new(window, cx, top)` with `top = (TITLEBAR_H + TAB_STRIP_H + 8) × ui_scale` (72 at 100%), and `AnimationDriver` (`cx.new(AnimationDriver::new)`, stored where `AnimationDriver::global` reads it, as `anim.rs` documents). Call `GlobalDemand` `set_main_window(window.window_handle().into())`. Subscribe: `TlSettings` (state version: mirror `history_mode` into `ShellState`, the tab strip and the toolbar model; `processes` version: toolbar model), window activation (toolbar model `window_active`). Select the start tab (below) without writing `last_tab`. Register the first-frame callback: `cx.on_next_frame(window, |this, window, cx| this.after_first_frame(window, cx))`. Entities and subscriptions are created only here.

`render`: first `GlobalHub` `note_render(cx)` (E16-003). Then `v_flex().size_full().bg(theme.window_bg).key_context("Global").track_focus(&self.root_focus)` with `.on_action` listeners for `SelectTab`, `NextTab`, `PrevTab`, `RefreshCurrentTab`, followed by the comment `// window-level on_action handlers (chain edits)`. Children: `self.titlebar.clone()` cached with `StyleRefinement::default().w_full().h(px(TITLEBAR_H * s))`; `self.tabstrip.clone()` cached with height `TAB_STRIP_H * s`; the page container `div().relative().flex_1().min_h_0()` holding the active slot's view `.cached(StyleRefinement::default().size_full())` (nothing when no page is built) and the status chip in `div().absolute().left_0().bottom_0().max_w(page_width - CHIP_RESERVE × s)` (cached). `render` creates nothing and allocates nothing besides the element tree.

Tab selection (`select_tab`, handlers for `SelectTab(i)`, `NextTab`, `PrevTab`):
- `SelectTab(i)` with `i` outside 0..=5 or a tab that is not built: nothing. The active tab: nothing.
- Switch: `set_active(false)` on the old page; create the new page on first visit through its factory and keep it; `set_active(true)`; update `active`, `ShellState.active_tab`, the tab strip, the toolbar (`titlebar.set_toolbar(model, toolbar_for(tab))`) and the status chip text; write `UiState.tabs.last_tab` through `TlSettings::update`; `focus_initial(Some(&primary_focus), &root_focus, ..)` (E20-007). The switch is instant (the P2 animation is E20-021).
- `NextTab` / `PrevTab`: the next or previous built tab, wrapping around.
- `RefreshCurrentTab`: calls the active page's `refresh`.
- Status text: on a page's `StatusChanged`, if that page is active, clear `status_buf`, call `status_text(&mut status_buf)` and pass it to `StatusChip::set_page_text`, and pass `status_actions()` to `StatusChip::set_page_actions`. Also on every tab switch.

First frame (`after_first_frame`, UI-SHL-110 step 11), in this order, each item a marked line:
1. Once per process (a `FirstFrameLogged` Global guards it, so a reopened window does not log again): read `/proc/self/stat` and `/proc/uptime` with `std::fs::read_to_string`, compute `first_frame_ms_from(..)` and log `tracing::info!(target: "tasklens::perf", first_frame_ms = ms, "first frame")`. On a read or parse failure log `warn!(target: "tasklens::perf", "first_frame_ms unavailable")`.
2. Comment lines in this order, for later beads to fill: `// step 11: queued toasts (E20-018)`, `// step 11: crash report (E20-018)`, `// step 11: --select-pid (E20-018)`, `// step 11: --start-minimized without tray (E20-018)`, `// step 11: helper unlock at launch (E20-026)`, `// step 11: public IP auto-fetch (E20-024)`.

`first_frame_ms_from(stat, uptime)`: split `stat` after the last `)` (the command name may contain spaces and parentheses); the remaining whitespace-separated fields start at field 3, so field 22 (`starttime`, clock ticks since boot) is the 20th of them. `start_ms = starttime × 10` (USER_HZ is 100 on Linux, fixed by the kernel ABI). `uptime` is "<seconds>.<hundredths> <idle>"; `now_ms = seconds × 1000 + hundredths × 10`. Result `now_ms.saturating_sub(start_ms)`; `None` on any parse failure.

