## Context
Anchor of E32. Finishes `tasklens --watch-memory`: the loop that waits on the PSI trigger and the 5 s `MemAvailable` check and starts `tasklens --low-memory` when the threshold is crossed and no rescue window from this watcher is open. The watcher does not start GPUI, targets under 4 MiB RSS, and calls `mlockall(MCL_CURRENT | MCL_FUTURE)`, which fits in systemd's default `RLIMIT_MEMLOCK` of 8 MiB. It coexists with systemd-oomd and never kills anything. With E32-001 and E32-002 this completes `watch_memory.rs` and `lowmem_unit.rs`. Sources: PROC-097, R-062, APP-052, UI-SHL-110 ("`--watch-memory` starts no GPUI").

