## Notes
- `rustix::mm::mlockall` needs rustix feature `mm`, which the ADR-002 workspace pin now has (R-142 item 5). `mlockall(MlockAllFlags)` is a safe function in rustix 1.1.5, so this bead needs no `unsafe`.
- Unprivileged PSI triggers: since Linux 6.5 an unprivileged trigger needs a window that is a multiple of 2 s, and older kernels need `CAP_SYS_RESOURCE`. `PSI_TRIGGER` is `full 200000 2000000` (10% over a 2 s window, R-151). When the write fails with `EINVAL` or `EPERM`, log `warn` once and run on the 5 s `MemAvailable` check only (`WaitResult::Timeout`); no second trigger string is tried. Use `rustix::event::poll` with `PollFlags::PRI`.
- The rescue child inherits the unit's environment and relies on the user manager's imported `WAYLAND_DISPLAY` or `DISPLAY`. When neither is set at trigger time, log `warn` and do not spawn. "No rescue window open" means the watcher's own child is alive (R-152 OI-6).
