## Context
`tasklens --watch-memory` is the low-memory watcher run by the user unit `tasklens-lowmem.service`. It starts the rescue window when memory pressure crosses a threshold. This bead writes the pure decision logic and the `MemAvailable` reader, with no I/O loop, so it can be tested without a real system. Sources: PROC-097, R-062, APP-052, ADR-004 (engine modes), ADR-001 (tl-app may not depend on tl-collect, so the watcher reads `/proc/meminfo` itself).

## Deliverable
`crates/tl-app/src/watch_memory.rs` (first part; E32-A1 adds the run loop to the same file). Only `std`, `rustix` and `tracing` are used, so the file can be included by path from an integration test.

```rust
/// PSI trigger written to /proc/pressure/memory: full stall above 10% over a 2 s window (R-062 as changed by R-151).
pub const PSI_TRIGGER: &str = "full 200000 2000000";
/// How often MemAvailable is checked (R-062).
pub const MEMAVAIL_CHECK: std::time::Duration = std::time::Duration::from_secs(5);
/// MemAvailable below this percent of MemTotal is critical (R-062).
pub const MEMAVAIL_MIN_PCT: u64 = 3;

#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct MemInfo { pub total_kib: u64, pub available_kib: u64 }

/// Parses the `MemTotal:` and `MemAvailable:` lines (value in kB). None if either is missing,
/// not a number, or MemTotal is 0. Never panics on any input.
pub fn parse_meminfo(buf: &[u8]) -> Option<MemInfo>;

/// true when available_kib * 100 < total_kib * MEMAVAIL_MIN_PCT (integer math, no floats).
pub fn mem_available_critical(m: &MemInfo) -> bool;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum WatchEvent { PsiTrigger, MemCheck(MemInfo), RescueExited }

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum WatchDecision { StartRescue, Nothing }

#[derive(Debug, Default)]
pub struct WatchState { rescue_running: bool }

impl WatchState {
    /// PsiTrigger, or MemCheck with a critical MemInfo, gives StartRescue only when no rescue
    /// window started by this watcher is running. RescueExited clears the running flag.
    pub fn on_event(&mut self, ev: WatchEvent) -> WatchDecision;
    /// Called after the rescue child was spawned.
    pub fn rescue_started(&mut self);
}
```

The watcher never kills anything itself (PROC-097). It only decides when to open the rescue window.

## Acceptance Criteria
- **Given** a meminfo text with `MemTotal: 16000000 kB` and `MemAvailable: 400000 kB` **When** `parse_meminfo` runs **Then** it returns `MemInfo { total_kib: 16000000, available_kib: 400000 }`.
- **Given** a meminfo text without a `MemAvailable:` line **When** `parse_meminfo` runs **Then** it returns `None`.
- **Given** `MemInfo { total_kib: 1000, available_kib: 29 }` **When** `mem_available_critical` runs **Then** it returns true.
- **Given** `MemInfo { total_kib: 1000, available_kib: 30 }` **When** `mem_available_critical` runs **Then** it returns false (3% exactly is not critical).
- **Given** a fresh `WatchState` **When** `on_event(PsiTrigger)` **Then** the result is `StartRescue`.
- **Given** a `WatchState` after `rescue_started()` **When** `on_event(PsiTrigger)` **Then** the result is `Nothing`.
- **Given** a `WatchState` after `rescue_started()` and `on_event(RescueExited)` **When** `on_event(PsiTrigger)` **Then** the result is `StartRescue`.
- **Given** a fresh `WatchState` **When** `on_event(MemCheck(m))` with a non-critical `m` **Then** the result is `Nothing`.

