```rust
/// Backend that maps paths to owning packages. Arch is the only v1 backend; `dpkg -S` and `rpm -qf` come in P4 behind the same trait.
pub trait PkgBackend: Send {
    /// One batched owner query. Returns (path, Some(name)) for owned paths, (path, None) for unowned ones.
    fn owners(&mut self, paths: &[&Path]) -> Result<Vec<(PathBuf, Option<Arc<str>>)>, CollectError>;
    /// Reads the package's metadata.
    fn info(&mut self, name: &str) -> Result<Option<PackageInfo>, CollectError>;
    /// PROC-078 integrity check.
    fn verify(&mut self, name: &str) -> Result<VerifyOutcome, CollectError>;
    /// Change marker of the package database (mtime of /var/lib/pacman/local).
    fn db_stamp(&mut self) -> Option<i64>;
}
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum VerifyOutcome { Unmodified, Modified { altered_files: u32 }, Failed(Arc<str>) }

pub struct Pacman { pub db_dir: PathBuf /* default /var/lib/pacman/local */ }
impl PkgBackend for Pacman { /* below */ }

pub const PKG_DEBOUNCE: Duration = Duration::from_secs(2);
pub const PKG_BATCH_MAX: usize = 256;

pub struct PackageIndex { /* cache: FxHashMap<(Arc<str> path, i64 mtime), Option<Arc<PackageInfo>>>, pending set, last_new: Instant, stamp: Option<i64>, backend: Box<dyn PkgBackend> */ }
impl PackageIndex {
    pub fn new(backend: Box<dyn PkgBackend>) -> Self;
    /// Cache lookup; never blocks. `None` = not looked up yet (the cell shows `…`), `Some(None)` = not packaged.
    pub fn get(&self, path: &str, mtime_s: i64) -> Option<Option<Arc<PackageInfo>>>;
    /// Queues a path that `get` did not know.
    pub fn request(&mut self, path: &str, mtime_s: i64, now: Instant);
    /// True when a batch is due: pending paths exist and PKG_DEBOUNCE passed since the last new one.
    pub fn due(&self, now: Instant) -> bool;
    /// Blocking: runs one batch of at most PKG_BATCH_MAX paths through the backend and fills the cache.
    /// Checks `db_stamp` first and clears the cache when it changed.
    pub fn run_batch(&mut self) -> Result<usize, CollectError>;
    /// Blocking: PROC-078 check for one package.
    pub fn verify(&mut self, name: &str) -> Result<VerifyOutcome, CollectError>;
}
```

`Pacman` rules:
- `owners`: runs `/usr/bin/pacman -Qo -- <paths…>` with `LC_ALL=C`, stdin null, stdout piped (at most 1 MiB read), and parses each stdout line `<path> is owned by <name> <version>`. A path that does not appear in stdout is `(path, None)`. Exit status 1 with some lines is normal (an unowned path). PROC-027 names `pacman -Qoq`; the `-q` form prints only names and cannot be mapped back to paths in a batch, so this bead uses `-Qo`.
- `info`: finds `<db_dir>/<name>-<version>/desc` by listing `db_dir` for entries that start with `<name>-` and whose `%NAME%` is `name`; parses the `%NAME%`, `%VERSION%`, `%DESC%`, `%PACKAGER%` (the name without the ` <email>` part), `%BUILDDATE%` (decimal seconds) and `%URL%` sections (a section is the `%KEY%` line followed by value lines up to a blank line). Read cap 64 KiB. Values are sanitized with `tl_collect::sanitize` before they are stored.
- `verify`: runs `/usr/bin/pacman -Qkk -- <name>` with `LC_ALL=C` and parses the summary line `<name>: <n> total files, <m> altered files`: `m == 0` gives `Unmodified`, else `Modified { altered_files: m }`; no summary line gives `Failed(<first stderr line, sanitized, at most 200 chars>)`.
- `db_stamp`: `statx` mtime of `db_dir`, `None` when it is missing.
- Commands run by fixed path, no shell, a 10 s wall limit (kill on expiry, then `Failed("timed out")`).

The index never runs on the sweep path: the sweep (E05-035) only calls `get` and `request`. The engine's Processes worker runs `run_batch` in its own `spawn_blocking` job when `due` is true, and the E10 detail worker runs `verify` for the Properties check (PROC-078).

